1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:01,261
This UPS driver just

2
00:00:01,261 --> 00:00:02,677
made 3 right turns...

3
00:00:02,677 --> 00:00:04,113
to avoid 1 left.

4
00:00:04,113 --> 00:00:05,433
Sounds ridiculous, right?

5
00:00:05,433 --> 00:00:06,524
But there's a reason.

6
00:00:06,524 --> 00:00:07,499
Meet Mike.

7
00:00:07,499 --> 00:00:08,533
He's got a truck full of

8
00:00:08,533 --> 00:00:10,517
packages and a computer-planned route.

9
00:00:10,517 --> 00:00:11,717
He spots a shortcut.

10
00:00:11,717 --> 00:00:12,739
One left turn.

11
00:00:12,739 --> 00:00:14,237
Straight to the next delivery.

12
00:00:14,237 --> 00:00:15,027
Easy.

13
00:00:15,027 --> 00:00:16,014
Except...

14
00:00:16,014 --> 00:00:17,271
the traffic doesn't stop.

15
00:00:17,271 --> 00:00:18,331
Cars keep coming.

16
00:00:18,331 --> 00:00:19,760
His engine keeps running.

17
00:00:19,760 --> 00:00:20,851
And Mike?

18
00:00:20,851 --> 00:00:22,148
He's going nowhere.

19
00:00:22,148 --> 00:00:23,634
That's why UPS factors

20
00:00:23,634 --> 00:00:26,127
left turns into its route calculations.

21
00:00:26,127 --> 00:00:27,683
An unnecessary left

22
00:00:27,683 --> 00:00:29,180
can get a 20-second penalty

23
00:00:29,180 --> 00:00:30,761
in UPS's route math.

24
00:00:30,761 --> 00:00:31,771
Not for the driver.

25
00:00:31,771 --> 00:00:32,758
For the route.

26
00:00:32,758 --> 00:00:33,524
So sometimes,

27
00:00:33,524 --> 00:00:35,753
3 right turns beat 1 left.

28
00:00:35,803 --> 00:00:37,102
And here's the crazy part.

29
00:00:37,102 --> 00:00:38,588
MythBusters actually tested this

30
00:00:38,588 --> 00:00:39,758
with a delivery truck.

31
00:00:39,758 --> 00:00:41,539
Their right-turn route was LONGER.

32
00:00:41,539 --> 00:00:43,049
But it used less fuel.

33
00:00:43,049 --> 00:00:45,081
And every mile counts.

34
00:00:45,081 --> 00:00:47,043
UPS says cutting just 1 mile

35
00:00:47,043 --> 00:00:48,575
per driver, per day,

36
00:00:48,575 --> 00:00:49,226
can save up to

37
00:00:49,226 --> 00:00:51,186
$50 million a year.

38
00:00:51,186 --> 00:00:53,255
So UPS doesn't ban left turns.

39
00:00:53,255 --> 00:00:55,264
If turning left makes more sense,

40
00:00:55,264 --> 00:00:56,814
the system can choose it.

41
00:00:56,814 --> 00:00:57,871
So Mike wasn't taking

42
00:00:57,871 --> 00:00:59,367
the long way by mistake.

43
00:00:59,367 --> 00:01:01,077
He was taking the smarter way.

44
00:01:01,077 --> 00:01:02,206
Because in delivery...

45
00:01:02,206 --> 00:01:03,019
The shortest route

46
00:01:03,019 --> 00:01:05,620
isn't always the cheapest.
